WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
Iceland sits where the North
American and Eurasian plates meet,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.010
and it is splitting apart.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.470
At Krafla, rifting opened about
7 metres between 1975 and 1984.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:18.330
On average, the ridge under the Atlantic
spreads about 2.5 centimetres a year.

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.090
Earth's rigid outer layer
is broken into plates,

6
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.930
all on the move.

7
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.450
Is Earth's spin flinging them apart?

8
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.230
Is the Moon pulling them?

9
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.270
What really moves them?

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.450
In this mission, you'll map the
three kinds of plate margin,

11
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.930
and see where earthquakes
and volcanoes cluster.

12
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.550
Then you'll follow a hotspot under Hawaii,

13
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.870
more than 3,200 kilometres
from the nearest boundary.

14
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.510
Your mission: find out
what drives the plates,

15
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.310
and weigh the evidence.
